  "title": "First Geneva Convention of 22 August 1864",
  "summary": "On 22 August 1864 a diplomatic conference in Geneva, convened by the Swiss Federal Council at the request of the ICRC, concluded the Convention for the Amelioration of the Condition of the Wounded in Armies in the Field. It required help for sick and wounded soldiers without discrimination and respect for medical staff, transport and equipment marked with the red cross.",
